This adds an API endpoint for validating a block without having the full
utxo set present. To validate a block in such a fashion, its block
header needs to be processed first. The spent coins are passed to the
function with a callback, which is invoked for each output spent by the
block (excluding outputs previously created by the block). The
introduced block validation function then validates the block through
`CheckBlock`, `ContextualCheckBlock`, and `ConnectBlock`.
</commits>

